The edges is a list of 1, 2, 3, 0, 0, 0.
The starts is a list of 0, 3, 4, 5.
The counts is a list of 3, 1, 1, 1.
The seen is a list of 64 zeros.
The queue is an empty list of whole numbers.
The depths is an empty list of whole numbers.
For every node from 0 to 3.
The startmask is shift 1 left by node.
The code is node times 16 plus startmask.
Set item code of seen to 1.
Place code into queue.
Place 0 into depths.

The head is 0.
The count is 4.
The answer is -1.
Repeat while head is less than count and answer is less than 0.
The state is item head of queue.
The distance is item head of depths.
Add 1 to head.
The node is state divided by 16.
The mask is state modulo 16.
For every offset from 0 to item node of counts minus 1.
The target is item (item node of starts plus offset) of edges.
The bit is shift 1 left by target.
The merged is bitwise or of mask and bit.
If merged is 15, set answer to distance plus 1, stop.
The code is target times 16 plus merged.
If item code of seen is 0.
Set item code of seen to 1.
Place code into queue.
Place distance plus 1 into depths.
Add 1 to count.

Show answer.
